ident. Or killed the cat!"}}, {"type": "objective", "content": "secondary_8"}]}], "type": "TYP", "id": 9, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " \nLaura is asking Mike about the accident.\n"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Quiz"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "\nInstructions: Listen to the audio. Type in the missing words.\n"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le17ob08re6aud03"}]}, {"type": "template_override", "content": 2}]}, {"stimuli_ids": [], "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"responses": [{"correct": 0, "selected": 0, "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}, {"correct": 1, "selected": 0, "id": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}]}], "type": "RSLT", "id": 10, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": []}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Quiz"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}]}, {"stimuli_ids": [], "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"responses": [{"correct": 1, "selected": 0, "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "pdf", "content": "engenn8le17ob08re7pdf01.pdf"}]}]}], "type": "DWS", "id": 11, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " \nTalk about all the things you have to do.\n"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Take Away"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "\nInstructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self Assessment.\n"}]}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}]}]}], "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "_data": []}, {"contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"coverimg": "engenn8le17ob08re2img05.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn8le17ob08re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "engenn8le17ob08re2img05.jpg", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn8le17ob08re2img05.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "Now, it's time to share a tale about a superstitious man from New Jersey. If I was his girlfriend, I wouldn't be holding hands with this guy in the near future!\n<br/><br/>\nA 25-year-old man, who was supposed to be taking his girlfriend to pick out engagement rings, caused a five-car pile up during rush hour. Richard Dalton, of New York, told detectives he fainted yesterday morning while holding his breath in the tunnel near the community of Bakersfield."}, {"time": "28000", "image": "engenn8le17ob08re2img01.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "His car drifted across the centerline and crashed head-on with a transport truck. Both vehicles struck the tunnel walls before veering into other traffic. Paramedics found victims comforting each other in the mayhem.  If it had not been for the quick action of other drivers at the scene, the accident could have ended in tragedy. During the investigation, police complained that some bystanders, who were supposed to remain behind the police tape, refused to let crews through, stood too close to the emergency vehicles and attempted to take photos on their cellphones."}, {"time": "61000", "image": "engenn8le17ob08re2img02.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "Dalton and his passenger girlfriend, suffered non-life-threatening injuries. Dalton was cited for reckless driving. Investigators state that if the health of any of the victim's declined in hospital, additional charges would be added.  A police lieutenant said he's not sure why Dalton was holding his breath. However, his girlfriend stated that her superstitious soul mate holds his breath in tunnels. \u201cAfter the accident, I was crossing my fingers that no one was seriously hurt,\u201d she said to police. \u201cWe were supposed to be getting married next week.\u201d In the end, the couple decided to part ways."}]}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": []}, {"contents": [{"type": "video", "value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"time": "5000", "image": "", "id": 1, "text": "Narrative Paragraph"}, {"time": "6000", "image": "", "id": 2, "text": "<span class = \"bullet\">How do you write a narrative?</span>"}, {"time": "70000", "image": "", "id": 3, "text": "<span class = \"bullet\">Verb tenses in narratives</span>"}, {"time": "97000", "image": "", "id": 4, "text": "<span class = \"bullet\">Linking verbs</span>"}], "video_src": "engenn8le17ob08re3vid01"}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "video", "id": 2, "_data": []}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Silly Superstitions"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Cross Your Fingers"}, {"type": "position", "content": 8}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 17}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Describe complicated or unusual events in the past through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn8le17ob08re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Writing a Narrative Paragraph"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " Narrative is the term for a story, long or short. It can be written about the past, present, or future. It may be factual or imagined."}, {"type": "text", "content": "A narrative needs characters, a setting and a clear problem to be interesting to an audience. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ol><li>Decide what type of story you are writing (mystery, fantasy, adventure).</li> <li>Decide who is the narrator (the person speaking).    </li> <li>Choose the characters and the setting (where and when). </li> <li>Write the problem or conflict. </li> <li>What happens at the end?</li></ol>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You often use these verbs in narratives to describe things that happened in the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "  <span class=\"strong\">Past tense </span><br/> Example:  <span class=\"italic\">The young man was terrified of walking under ladders.</span>  <br/> <span class=\"strong\">Past Continuous tense </span><br/> Example:  <span class=\"italic\">Jonathan was walking home late at night when he saw a black cat cross his path. </span> <br/>  <span class=\"strong\">Past Perfect tense</span><br/>  Example:  <span class=\"italic\">He had always avoided going through tunnels.</span> <br/>  <span class=\"strong\">Past Perfect Continuous tense</span><br/>  Example: <span class=\"italic\"> It had been raining for days.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Linking words help to structure a narrative and connect ideas.  They help to provide a sequence of events."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use words like:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"During\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Soon\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Immediately\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Once\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"As soon as\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Finally\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"In the end\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"At last\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"At last\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "During the investigation, police complained that some bystanders, who were supposed to remain behind the police tape, refused to let crews through."}, {"type": "example", "content": "In the end, the couple decided to part ways."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Conditional Sentences with <span class=\"italic\">If</span> Clause"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " There are two kinds of conditional sentences: real and unreal. The Real Conditional describes real-life situations. The Unreal Conditional describes unreal, imaginary situations."}, {"type": "text", "content": "    Zero conditional sentences have two present simple verbs,  one in the <span class=\"italic\">if</span> clause and one in the  main clause. You use this conditional when the result will always happen."}, {"type": "text", "content": " You use the form: <br/>If + present simple, ... present simple."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the first conditional with <span class=\"italic\">if</span> clauses to exchange opinions about possible future outcomes."}, {"type": "text", "content": "  You use the form: <br/> If + present simple, ... will + infinitive"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the second conditional to exchange opinions about unreal or imaginary (hypothetical) situations in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the form: <br/>If + past simple, ... would + infinitive"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the third conditional to talk about the past. It is used to describe a situation that didn't happen, and to imagine the result of this situation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "If + past perfect, ... would + have + past participle"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If I were his girlfriend, I wouldn't be holding hands with this guy in the near future!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If it had not been for the quick action of other drivers at the scene, the accident could have ended in tragedy."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Investigators stated that if the health of any of the victims declined in hospital, additional charges would be added."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to faint"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to lose consciousness temporarily"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Richard Dalton fainted yesterday morning."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le17ob08aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use in a story about superstitions and manners."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pile up"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a collision of multiple cars"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He caused a five-car pile up during rush hour."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le17ob08aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "tunnel"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an underground passage, especially for cars or trains"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He was holding his breath in the tunnel near Bakersfield."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le17ob08aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to drift"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to deviate from a regular course"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: His car drifted across the centerline."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le17ob08aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to veer"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to change direction of course"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Both vehicles struck the walls before veering into other traffic."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le17ob08aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "mayhem"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "random damage"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Victims comforted each other in the mayhem."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le17ob08aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to cite"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to call to a public audience"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Dalton was cited because of the accident he caused."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le17ob08aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "reckless"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " careless; irresponsible"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Dalton's reckless driving caused the accident."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le17ob08aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "soulmate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person, friend or couple, who completely understands another person"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Dalton's girlfriend said her soulmate holds his breath in tunnels."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le17ob08aud09"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "crew"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a group of people who work together, in the police, as doctors, etc."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Bystanders refused to let crews through."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le17ob08aud10"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Pretend it is Halloween, and you have lots to do, but you are very busy."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use \u201csupposed to\" and \"not supposed to\" to make a list of 5 sentences about all the things you need to do, but didn't."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Then use \u201c If I had \u2026 \u201c to talk about all the things you would do if you had more time."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Compare with a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Edit each other's sentences."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I talk about manners, customs and superstitions."}, {"type": "text", "content": " I talk about things I was supposed to do and things that were supposed to happen."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about hypothetical situations."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I edit other people's work."}]}]}